                <pb facs="0478" n="362" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">738.3915/257: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">W. W. Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-09-14T00:00:00-04:40"><hi rendition="#italic">September 14,
                                1923—12 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 16—8:15
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>50. I had long conference yesterday with the President and Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs in regard to the boundary question. The President is taking active steps
                    in the matter and I hope that within a short time something will have been
                    accomplished as to the naming of arbiters to begin negotiations at Port au
                    Prince.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
